Key Stages of a CI/CD Pipeline
• Source Stage: A developer pushes code to a shared repository like GitHub, which
automatically triggers the pipeline.
• Build Stage: The system compiles code and packages dependencies or container
images using tools like Docker.
• Test Stage: Automated unit and integration tests check the code for bugs and
security vulnerabilities.
• Release/Deploy Stage: Approved builds move to staging or production
